            <div type="commentary">
                <p><!--commented out pending revision-->
                    <!--lists allocation of plots of land (called 'thema' or 'themelion') to individuals with generally standard Greek names, by local locational descriptions. Ocassionally various other towns are mentioned, as ethnics on the ends of someone's name; name in l.40 is strange (Kannei? Kanneius? Kaibel appears to sugg. Archedamus Archedami f. Cannensis! P-C argues that these are ethnics of Akrai pagi rather than of other cities - 'e poco probabile che suolo verisimilmente pubblico venisse assegnato a stranieri', and cf. the TLAs attached to mag. names in other Akrai inscrs. Some of the named individuals occur also in other Akrai inscrs. P-C suggests, on the letter-forms, that IG 208 and 211 are contemporary with this one, IG 210 is of a diff. date.--></p>
            </div>
